Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: VU1's last microcode uploads and program starts, dumped on a reserved instruction

Always on, a few stores each: the last 256 MPG uploads that changed VU1's code (with an FNV hash of their bytes) or were
dropped (their data past the transfer) - an unchanged upload counted on the newest entry for the same place - and the last
256 program starts (MSCAL / MSCALF / MSCNT, a run of the same start counted on one entry), one sequence number ordering
both. When VU1 meets a reserved instruction (the fast engine's report or the reference interpreter's), they are written
to runs/vu1_uploads_<n>.txt (the first 4 times in a session) with the code around the pc, beside PS2X_VU1_HISTORY's
vu1_history.txt (which records every instruction and so stays off).

For Transformers (TODO 185 b): a player's game stopped after a warp tunnel in which VU1 kept starting at 0x270 / 0x1408
on words 0xFFFFFFFB; not reproduced in eight tunnels on the test PC - the next one shows what wrote that code.

ps2xRuntime:
- ps2_vif1_interpreter.cpp: the two rings, filled at MPG / MSCAL / MSCALF / MSCNT; ps2Vu1RingDump.
- vu/ps2_vu1_fast.cpp, vu/ps2_vu1_core.cpp: the reserved-instruction reports call it.

